---
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>

<div class="content article-page">

            <!-- Title -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h1>👷 My Profit Land – Beginner Guide (Worker Path)</h1>
                <p class="meta">Author: <span>Mina Nashaat</span> | Published: Feb 2026</p>
            </div>

             <div class="card">
                <img class="article-image" src="imgs/work.png" alt="War Specialist Update">
            </div>

            <!-- Introduction -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <p>
                    If you are new to <strong>My Profit Land</strong>, the first thing you should do is read the
                    <strong>Terms and Conditions</strong> carefully. This is a real-money game,
                    and following the rules is extremely important to protect your account and your earnings.
                </p>
                <p>
                    If you are joining as an investor, you may skip this guide. However,
                    reading it is still recommended, since understanding the worker system
                    helps you better understand the game economy.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h2>🔹 Step 1: Start Working</h2>
                <p>After completing registration and full verification:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Go to <strong>Activity</strong></li>
                    <li>Click on <strong>Work</strong></li>
                    <li>Press the <strong>Work</strong> button at the top of the company</li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    Each work shift lasts <strong>4 hours</strong>,
                    and you can work up to <strong>3 shifts per day</strong>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Beginner Strategy -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h2>📅 Beginner Strategy (First Days)</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Work <strong>2 shifts per day</strong></li>
                    <li>After 3 days, receive the <strong>Government Work Bonus</strong></li>
                    <li>Use the <strong>Homeless Shelter</strong> for 10% free energy</li>
                </ul>

                <p><strong>Important:</strong> Do NOT buy energy products, including mansions.</p>
                <p>
                    The increasing cost of energy will not be profitable in the early stage.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Exception:</strong> Every third day, just before receiving the government bonus,
                    you may buy <strong>one Great Wine</strong>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Economic Score -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h2>📊 Understanding Economic Score (ES)</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Work twice per day → ES increases by <strong>+1</strong> </li>
                    <li>Work once per day → ES stays the same</li>
                    <li>No work → ES decreases by <strong>-1</strong></li>
                    <li>Maximum ES is <strong>100</strong></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- Overshifts -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h2>🚀 When to Start Over time shifts?</h2>
                <p>
                    After about a month, when your ES reaches <strong>30–40</strong>
                    and you can log in more frequently, you may start considering overshifts.
                </p>
                <p>
                    After reaching <strong>50 ES</strong>, overshifts are usually profitable.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Only buy enough energy to reach the <strong>55% minimum requirement</strong>
                    needed to activate overshifts.
                </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Final Advice -->
            <div class="card article-card-spacing">
                <h2>⚖️ Final Advice</h2>
                <p>
                    The worker path requires patience and discipline.
                    Focus on steady ES growth, control your energy spending,
                    and avoid unnecessary expenses.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Master the basics first — profit comes later.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>

</Layout>
